{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/231227-discussion-of-future-supplements","id":231227,"title":"Discussion of Future Supplements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-17T02:56:09-07:00","id":231227,"title":"Discussion of Future Supplements","content":"I figure starting up a thread about future ideas for Onyx Path would be a good way to go of it. Even though Stew &amp; Co. are swamped with W20 stuff I'd dig seeing Second Edition get a full treatment for everything. I figure a Book on the Shadow will come out for the default &quot;blue-book&quot; line like Hurt-Locker so I'll leave that there.<br /> <br /> Book of Packs: Seems a pretty solid idea for a book. The core of the Uratha experience revolves around their pack, and new merits/gifts/rites focusing on this special connection seems good enough for focused treatment. I'd think touching on different examples of Pack layouts around the world would also be good for a chapter. I'm personally interested in seeing non-Totem spirits being part of your Pack, and even animals are included in Gifts and a sidebar. With the Dead Wolf Bloodline from Vampire and the Spiritus Transmutation from Promethean even non-Mortal people should probably have cases of joining the group.<br /> <br /> Book of Prey: What can I say? I frickin' love Predators, and if what the freelancers have said about Dread Powers and the like they don't have enough room in the corebook and would like to do more. Spirits, Claimed, Hosts, and Ancient Horrors that are outside the norm should make a return with new ideas and new ways to put them out in GMC. The Idigam are going to be in the core, but that doesn't stop them from adding even more to this book. What can I say? I like options!<br /> <br /> Book of Lore: I frickin' love magic. Its the thing that keeps making me think of the major place of Werewolves in any setting. The shapeshifting ties them to being monsters and predators, but the magic makes me think of them being something &quot;more&quot; than what's normally seen fiction. Exploring what that magic is, be it Gifts, Rites, or Fetishes, will help to cement it in my mind and give more ideas on how each character can view who and what they are and what they can do.<br /> <br /> Book on Hunting Grounds: It seems a solid space to expand on territories around the world and how the history and locals have an effect on the Shadow and traditions of the People. Also, if the Hunting Grounds are all like the Australian example that was spoiled they should help ever ST to develop their own locations and customize them.<br /> <br /> One thing I felt First Edition was weird about what how they shoved the Tribes/Auspices into singular books with relatively lopsided treatments. Right now you have to read Lore of the Forsaken, The Rage, and Tribes of the Moon/Signs of the Moon for a look at the Tribes and Auspices and the differing views of each and how they can fit. And the refocusing on the Hunt and what this means to each Tribe(and the Uratha's place on the Hunt in relation to their Auspice) as Prey makes me thinks each deserves a retread. <br /> <br /> Rather than cramming everything into a single book I'd rather each one stood on its own as a window into one of the core aspects of the splat. Its a new edition and I want more books. Pretty simple on that front. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Right there we have about 13 books. Great for any Edition run. The Tribe and Auspice books probably don't need to be overly long, but I figure the Books on Prey/Packs/Lore should hit the 160-200 mark.<br /> <br /> What would other people like to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T03:14:53-07:00","id":231255,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunting Grounds. Hunting Grounds. Hunting Grounds.</b><br /> <br /> The equivalent chapter in <i>B&amp;S</i> was the highlight of the book for me, and I'm in love with what we've seen of them in WtF 2e so far. More of them would be super welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T03:25:13-07:00","id":231257,"title":"","content":"<b>Maeljin and the Bale Hounds.</b> This is more of a &quot;what would you want from the book when it comes out,&quot; since Stew has said he's got <i>something</i> in the pipeline for 2e Bale Hounds. So here's my headspace: Tell me why it's cool and interesting that spirits across the Hisil know the name &quot;Maeljin,&quot; though it is foreign to the First Tongue, because &quot;an easter egg from Apocalypse&quot; ain't gonna cut it. Alternately, rename them if you like, that's cool too. Werewolves occupy an interesting niche as the critters among the World of Darkness, I think, whose concerns are closest to those of the Inferno. Mages have a name for it because they like naming things they didn't already have names for, but the Inferno isn't an active presence in the life of the Awakened to any extent greater than other threatening and strange elements of the Fallen World are. Werewolves? Werewolves have to look over their back for an entire secret tribe of infiltrators in praise of the Pit, and Wounds are at least common enough in the Shadow Realm that they have a common term for them and a vague understanding of what they are and who dwells therein. I want to see a book that works with that, tells me why that is. Not only in terms of why it is that Wounds develop and spirits turn to the Maeljin, but in an out of character, thematic way: tell me why Hell on Earth is a theme appropriate to Forsaken. Connect me to the old myths that conflate werewolves, witches and Satanists. I'm not generally a big fan of the &quot;Lower Depths&quot; / &quot;Inferno&quot; stuff, but the Bale Hounds are cool, and they're also a strong conduit through which to convince me that the Inferno is cool, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T03:28:32-07:00","id":231260,"title":"","content":"Stoked with the kind words for the Hunting Grounds. While I can't give details about the others, I can say that anyone reading the breadth of ideas in WtF 2nd edition should have no trouble generating ideas of their own.<br /> <br /> They're very welcome to use the Grounds as they are, of course. I've got The Red Centre and [REDACTED] that I really want to hear tales from players making them their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T07:47:56-07:00","id":231497,"title":"","content":"Can we possibly get an add on write up update on bale hound gifts similar to the treatment the pure are getting? I'm fine with sticking to blasphemies, but I feel their gift list won't work with the new system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T09:23:07-07:00","id":231588,"title":"","content":"I'd happily do such a thing; we'll see what Stew has in mind for scheduling add-on write-ups, and by who.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T04:07:31-07:00","id":232654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/231227-discussion-of-future-supplements?p=231497#post231497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we possibly get an add on write up update on bale hound gifts similar to the treatment the pure are getting? I'm fine with sticking to blasphemies, but I feel their gift list won't work with the new system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we can. <br /> <br /> As for future books, Prey/Lore/Hunting Grounds mirrors in some ways the initial Forsaken releases. I'm not saying it's a bad pattern, but I can think of a few ways to improve on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:25:51-07:00","id":233497,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I figured it would mirror First Edition's releases too closely while I was writing. Its why I started the thread to see other ideas people would have. Didn't think the Dev/Writers would jump in. XD<br /> <br /> Hmmm, how about combining the Tribes and Prey book into a single volume each. This is who we are, and what we believe. Seems like a good place to have a particular target tied with the mythos of a group. Bone Shadows also being the book about Spirit Antagonists, Hunters in Darkness being the book on Hosts, etc. Blood Talons are something of a problem in this set-up because I figure they can't also be the book on Pure. Just spitballing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:47:54-07:00","id":234143,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of Vampire's clanbooks (in-character stories in the front, some mechanics in the back). Something similar for Werewolf would be great (some scholar or diplomat going around and trying to get the feel of the various tribes, perhaps at the behest of a lodge seeking out information). Particularly considering the 1e approach really had a lot more background information compared to mechanics, and the background was occasionally doled out in a bland fashion.<br /> <br /> Another way to do it, though this might make for a very wanted book, might be to have the Bale Hounds and the Pure in the same book, along with some of the other outsider factions, as they're all Werewolves, just not the Forsaken kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-19-2014, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T04:02:36-07:00","id":235285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/231227-discussion-of-future-supplements?p=233497#post233497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I figured it would mirror First Edition's releases too closely while I was writing. Its why I started the thread to see other ideas people would have. Didn't think the Dev/Writers would jump in. XD<br /> <br /> Hmmm, how about combining the Tribes and Prey book into a single volume each. This is who we are, and what we believe. Seems like a good place to have a particular target tied with the mythos of a group. Bone Shadows also being the book about Spirit Antagonists, Hunters in Darkness being the book on Hosts, etc. Blood Talons are something of a problem in this set-up because I figure they can't also be the book on Pure. Just spitballing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to post more, rather than just reading. Doesn't hurt that SA was down when I checked this morning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm interested in what people want to see, but I don't want to talk about individual ideas just yet. That way, it doesn't start looking like I'm confirming anything. I can't say anything about our plans beyond next August. So please, keep sharing your ideas. I'll also pose this as the question to the next blog entry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T12:03:52-07:00","id":235617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/231227-discussion-of-future-supplements?p=233497#post233497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I figured it would mirror First Edition's releases too closely while I was writing. Its why I started the thread to see other ideas people would have. Didn't think the Dev/Writers would jump in. XD<br /> <br /> Hmmm, how about combining the Tribes and Prey book into a single volume each. This is who we are, and what we believe. Seems like a good place to have a particular target tied with the mythos of a group. Bone Shadows also being the book about Spirit Antagonists, Hunters in Darkness being the book on Hosts, etc. Blood Talons are something of a problem in this set-up because I figure they can't also be the book on Pure. Just spitballing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think it'd be better to just base the books of the tribal themes, not really having a ton of prey books. Just having one Tribe be the focus of the fiction and art in the &quot;selected&quot; book,<br /> Iron Masters for a 2e Blood of the Wolf, with focus on mortals and wolf-bloods in the pack<br /> Bone Shadows for spirits and mysticism, Lore 2.0, basically.<br /> Hunters in Darkness for an updated Territories.<br /> Blood Talons for general prey book, sure, all the Tribes hunt, but the Talons are the warriors. So Predators revised.<br /> Storm Lords, finally, I'd go for a book about politics and so on. <br /> <br /> Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:27:44-07:00","id":236928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/231227-discussion-of-future-supplements?p=231257#post231257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Maeljin and the Bale Hounds.</b> This is more of a &quot;what would you want from the book when it comes out,&quot; since Stew has said he's got <i>something</i> in the pipeline for 2e Bale Hounds. So here's my headspace: Tell me why it's cool and interesting that spirits across the Hisil know the name &quot;Maeljin,&quot; though it is foreign to the First Tongue, because &quot;an easter egg from Apocalypse&quot; ain't gonna cut it. Alternately, rename them if you like, that's cool too. Werewolves occupy an interesting niche as the critters among the World of Darkness, I think, whose concerns are closest to those of the Inferno. Mages have a name for it because they like naming things they didn't already have names for, but the Inferno isn't an active presence in the life of the Awakened to any extent greater than other threatening and strange elements of the Fallen World are. Werewolves? Werewolves have to look over their back for an entire secret tribe of infiltrators in praise of the Pit, and Wounds are at least common enough in the Shadow Realm that they have a common term for them and a vague understanding of what they are and who dwells therein. I want to see a book that works with that, tells me why that is. Not only in terms of why it is that Wounds develop and spirits turn to the Maeljin,<b> but in an out of character, thematic way: tell me why Hell on Earth is a theme appropriate to Forsaken.</b> Connect me to the old myths that conflate werewolves, witches and Satanists. I'm not generally a big fan of the &quot;Lower Depths&quot; / &quot;Inferno&quot; stuff, but the Bale Hounds are cool, and they're also a strong conduit through which to convince me that the Inferno is cool, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This this <i>this</i>. Especially the bolded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T12:18:27-07:00","id":245550,"title":"","content":"And updated Predators book with updated rules for the spirits, claimed, host, etc. One of the best books in NWoD publication. This would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:01:28-07:00","id":246178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/231227-discussion-of-future-supplements?p=236928#post236928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This this <i>this</i>. Especially the bolded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Forsaken play largely the role o